# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## Project Overview

A Christmas date simulation game ("かおりと福岡クリスマス") built with Expo/React Native. The player explores Fukuoka's Christmas spots with their cousin "Kaori" (雪村かおり), earning points through check-ins and building affection through dialogue choices.

## Commands

```bash
# Development
npm start              # Start Expo dev server
npm run ios            # iOS simulator
npm run android        # Android emulator
npm run web            # Web browser

# Testing
npm test               # Run all tests
npm test -- --watch    # Watch mode
npm test -- path/to/test.ts  # Single test file

# Code Quality
npm run typecheck      # TypeScript check (tsc --noEmit)
npm run lint           # ESLint
npm run lint:fix       # ESLint with auto-fix
```

## Architecture

### Routing (Expo Router - file-based)
```
app/
├── _layout.tsx     # Root: ClerkProvider + GameProvider wrapper
├── index.tsx       # Title screen
├── opening.tsx     # Prologue story
├── main.tsx        # Main VN-style gameplay screen (GPS-based backgrounds, chat input)
├── (auth)/         # Auth routes (sign-in, sign-up)
├── map.tsx         # Spot list + OpenStreetMap view
├── spot/[id].tsx   # Dynamic spot detail
├── event.tsx       # Visual novel event scenes with choices
├── chat.tsx        # Standalone chat screen
├── ending.tsx      # Multi-ending (BAD/NORMAL/GOOD/TRUE based on score)
└── share.tsx       # SNS share functionality
```

### State Management
- **GameContext** (`src/contexts/GameContext.tsx`): Central game state (score, affection, checkedInSpots, timeRemaining)
- Score thresholds: BAD <600, NORMAL <1200, GOOD <1800, TRUE >=1800
- 9-hour fixed game duration
- Affection levels 1-5 affect Kaori's speech patterns (formal → casual)

### Key Components
- **CharacterDisplay** (`src/components/CharacterDisplay.tsx`): Character sprite rendering with expression support (neutral/happy/shy/surprised/sad/thinking), emoji fallback on load failure
- **useNearestSpot** (`src/hooks/useNearestSpot.ts`): GPS tracking hook with Haversine distance calculation, 500m threshold for spot detection
- **useActivityTracking** (`src/hooks/useActivityTracking.ts`): Pedometer integration (100 steps = 1 point)

### Data & Constants
- **SPOT_DATA** (`src/constants/character.ts`): 9 Fukuoka spots (6 normal + 3 secret) with coordinates and event scripts
- **HONORIFIC_LEVELS**: Affection-based speech pattern system
- **generateKaoriSystemPrompt()**: Dynamic AI prompt generator based on affection level

### Backend Integration
- **Supabase** (`src/services/supabase.ts`): PostgreSQL backend for users, spots, checkins, chat_logs
- **Clerk** (optional): Authentication with 10s timeout fallback to guest mode

## Testing

Tests are in `__tests__/` directory:
- `unit/`: Core logic tests (character, gameLogic, ai, dependencies)
- `integration/`: End-to-end flows
- Setup: `__tests__/setup.ts` mocks console and fetch

## Environment Variables

Required in `.env.local`:
```
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=  # Optional, enables auth
```

## Visual Novel UI Pattern

The main screen (`app/main.tsx`) follows visual novel conventions:
- Bottom dialogue box with speaker name
- Character sprite positioned above dialogue area
- GPS-based background switching (day/night, per-spot)
- Chat input integrated into main UI (no separate screen navigation)
- Expression parsing: AI responses include `[expression:xxx]` tags
